1790668027.037	Before Johannes Gutenberg perfected his system around 1450, the concept of mass textual reproduction existed in various forms across different cultures. These early methods were characterized by manual labor or rudimentary mechanical aids, but they established the fundamental human desire for reproducible text.
1790668027.037	
